            <ArticleTitle>Glomus tumour: a rare differential for subungual lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2014-209085</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2014209085</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 21-year-old, usually fit and well man, presented with a 10-year history of intermittent, paroxysmal pain and temperature sensitivity to his right thumb. He felt this was associated with a subungual lesion present on the same digit. He was diagnosed as having a glomus tumour and was referred to the hand surgeons for surgical excision.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
